sec.p:
Here, the amount of calcein released into the in vitro medium indicated the stability of niosomes as drug carriers. The lesser the calcein amount released, the more stable the niosome system. For this evaluation, it was necessary to compare it with the liposomal system, which is easily degraded in the digestive tract. The level of calcein released into the medium was determined by considering the correction due to dilution during the test procedure. The measured calcein levels were corrected using the Wurster equation [45].\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
